{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"64a7517b-d593-44a3-b533-9a46e3fcd3f7","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Flip two fair coins independently. The first coin starts our tree: heads or tails, each with probability one half.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Two fair coin flips"},{"op":"figure","id":"tree","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.5,6.2],"y":[-3.3,3.3],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"first_h","at":[2,1.6],"label":"H"},{"kind":"point","id":"first_t","at":[2,-1.6],"label":"T"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"start"},"to":{"at":"first_h"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"start"},"to":{"at":"first_t"},"label":"1/2"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"64a7517b-d593-44a3-b533-9a46e3fcd3f7","step":{"id":"s2","script":"After heads, the second coin can still land heads or tails. Multiply probabilities along a path: one half times one half equals one quarter.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"heads_paths","on":"tree","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"hh","at":[4.3,2.6],"label":"HH"},{"kind":"point","id":"ht","at":[4.3,0.8],"label":"HT"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"first_h"},"to":{"at":"hh"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"first_h"},"to":{"at":"ht"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"text","at":[5.5,2.6],"text":"1/4"},{"kind":"text","at":[5.5,0.8],"text":"1/4"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"multiply","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"P(HH)=\\frac12\\times\\frac12=\\frac14"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"64a7517b-d593-44a3-b533-9a46e3fcd3f7","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The tails branch splits the same way. We now have four equally likely outcomes; each complete path has probability one quarter.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"tails_paths","on":"tree","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"th","at":[4.3,-0.8],"label":"TH"},{"kind":"point","id":"tt","at":[4.3,-2.6],"label":"TT"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"first_t"},"to":{"at":"th"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"first_t"},"to":{"at":"tt"},"label":"1/2"},{"kind":"text","at":[5.5,-0.8],"text":"1/4"},{"kind":"text","at":[5.5,-2.6],"text":"1/4"}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What is the probability of tails first, then heads?","expected_gist":"1/4: multiply the two branch probabilities."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"64a7517b-d593-44a3-b533-9a46e3fcd3f7","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Exactly one head happens on two paths: heads then tails, or tails then heads. Add these separate outcomes to get one half.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"highlight","on":"tree","marks":[{"kind":"circle","center":{"at":"ht"},"r":0.35},{"kind":"circle","center":{"at":"th"},"r":0.35}]},{"op":"text","id":"one_head","anchor":{"el":"multiply","side":"below","gap":0.12},"content":"Exactly one head: HT or TH"},{"op":"equation","id":"add_paths","anchor":{"el":"one_head","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P(\\text{exactly one head})=\\frac14+\\frac14=\\frac12"}],"checkpoint":null}}
